-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- the certificate checker over Int
-- An integer code: literals, variables, sums and negations. Its value at an environment of
-- differences is a difference (coordinatewise: a negation swaps the coordinates). The checker
-- translates: a variable v becomes the two word variables 2v (the positive coordinate) and
-- 2v+1 (the negative one), a code becomes the pair of word codes of its coordinates, and the
-- claim a ≤ b (that is, a⁺ + b⁻ ≤ b⁺ + a⁻ as words) becomes the word claim lib/linproof.cub's
-- cert-check decides. Soundness is cert-sound transported along the translation.
data IntCode = ic-lit (z : Int) | ic-var (v : Word) | ic-add (a : IntCode) (b : IntCode) | ic-neg (a : IntCode)
